Relying on results due to Shmerkin and Solomyak, we show that outside a $0$-dimensional set of parameters, for every planar homogeneous self-similar measure $
u$, with strong separation, dense rotations and dimension greater than $1$, there exists $q>1$ such that $\{P_{z}
u\}_{z\in S}\subset L^{q}(\mathbb{R})$. Here $S$ is the unit circle and $P_{z}w=\left\langle z,wightangle $ for $w\in\mathbb{R}^{2}$. We then study such measures. For instance, we show that $
u$ is dimension conserving in each direction and that the map $zightarrow P_{z}
u$ is continuous with respect to the weak topology of $L^{q}(\mathbb{R})$.
